Professional Case Narrative

A male patient in his 50s developed liver failure after self-medicating with paracetamol 8 g/day for approximately six months for chronic back pain. He required hospitalization for a life-threatening hepatic event. Paracetamol was withdrawn, followed by recovery with sequelae. A positive rechallenge was subsequently reported, with recurrence of liver failure. The reporter assessed the causal relationship as certain. No alternative causes were reported. Based on the available information, this case represents a valid and serious ICSR with a WHO-UMC causality assessment of Certain.
